A||N||14||AusFiero||Would T-Top Rubbers Be Worth Reproducing ?||||1||
Z||000000||AusFiero||06-03-2001||04:36 AM||||I was just wondering, and I haven't looked into how it would be done yet either. But would there be a market for reproduction t-top rubbers, considering the low volumes originally produced?<P>Asking because I still have a brand new set of t-top rubbers sitting at home and know they are pretty much non existent now. If feasible cost wise and if the market is big enough I might see one of our local rubber gurus about reproducing them.<P>Would there be enough interest?<BR>Parts dealers please feel free to throw your 2c worth in as to make it feasible it is probably you guys I would need to sell them to.<P>I have looked into the feasibility though of reproducing the glass as I got stung big time replacing one of mine. The glass is not cheap though as it would work out about US$300 a side just to manufacture, without allowing for a profit or shipping. The glass is probably better remanufactured in the USA.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>When I was young I spent 80% of my money on Women, Gambling and Alcohol. I guess I wasted the rest.||||reg||1
Z||000001||skitime||06-03-2001||08:24 AM||||Please try to get the rubber seals made. The t-top community would be forever indepted.<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL><BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pictures-1_5.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||turbo86se||06-03-2001||10:34 AM||||Skitime, you're absolutely right. We'd all be in debt to you, AusFiero. I really need a set. <P>Is there a difference between the CJB 88 seals and the 84-87 seals? I've got the CJB, and I know skitime does too on his beautiful GT (trade?)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>What year are the seals for Aus?<BR>TIA! <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||AusFiero||06-03-2001||10:44 AM||||Good question on the fit. I know when I bought mine my top arrived as the wrong type making it an 88 top which seems to function fine on my 86 and the old 86 rubber went straight on it. The 88 as far as I can tell has one extra rib in the metal trim section? <P>My top was fitted in the second half of 86 making it one of the earlier conversions.<P>Anyone know if  the rubbers are the same even though the tops differ slightly?<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||06-03-2001||12:24 PM||||Mine are in pretty good shape except for the one piece that is on the very outside above the drivers window. Actually it looks like it is in good shape but it is coming loose at the top and I have to stick it back up in there every now and then...<P>But yes, if someone could reproduce an affordable set I would buy them and replace everything when I redo the car soon. Was kinda hating the idea of having everything new on the car except those anyway.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif"> <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A>||||reg||14
