Z||000009||Raydar||06-03-2001||04:58 PM||||Aus, You have mail!<P>The 88 CJB rubber seals are different from the earlier versions. <BR>This includes the seal that starts at A-pillar by the mirror, goes all the way around the hatch opening, and ends at the bottom of the B-pillar. There is also a difference in the seal at the outside edge of the glass hatch. <BR>I'm not sure what the differences are, but I'm told that the 88 seals will work with the earlier installations. The T-frame and glass seals will need to be replaced at the same time. In other words the old hatch seal is not compatible with the new T-frame seal, etc.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"||||reg||1
Z||000010||Huck||06-03-2001||10:53 PM||||I would by the seals in a minute!  Mine are done right now, passenger side leaks bad.  I need to order some, but dont know where.  None of the auto glass shops around here want to touch it.. they tell me that they can put them in if I find the seals.<P>  1 question though.  How do you know what seals you need? I have an 87GT that I bought last summer, but I have no idea when the T's were put in, or who did them.  I am actually worried they may just be a hack job.<P>Huck<BR>87 GT T-top||||reg||1
Z||000011||AusFiero||06-03-2001||11:03 PM||||Ok fesibility study started. Have contacted a manufacturer and the fesibility is there. It would mean I would have to buy 100 sets though.<P>Price will always be a decider and they would not be cheap due to the custom nature of a small production. But already have worked out they would cost (ballpark figure) about US$500 a set. A set being 2 main seals and the seals on the glass assembly itself either side. The P Seals would not be included at that price.<P>Still any interest or would I be wasting my time continueing to look into this? I would need to have confirmed orders for 70 to 100 sets to even consider continueing as I would be looking at laying out nearly $80,000 AUS to do it. Thats a second mortgage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">||||reg||1
